Kubernetes node-maintenance image

Supported operations are fixed: node-recovery (read-only), exact-entry
network-repair, kexec-recovery-validate (validation only), and kexec-recovery
(controller-drained reboot into a digest-pinned provider bundle).
and hotfix-action (one controller-rendered, four-eyes platform hotfix).
Controller-owned node, full repair-tuple approval, operation, and recording
bindings are required. No broad neighbor/FDB flush, caller command, argument, path, image,
unrestricted shell, caller-selected kernel, or general-purpose toolbox is supported.
Read the generic runbooks in
/usr/share/breakglass/runbooks/upstream/node-maintenance/ before use.
An optional deployment-specific, read-only OCI runbook bundle may be mounted
at /usr/share/breakglass/runbooks/internal/. A selected bundle must contain
bundle.yaml and INDEX.md and is not sourced or executed by this image.
